{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>If you take as pledge.</b> It appears that it alludes to arouse the slumbering man in whose hand is the garment of him concerning whom Scripture said (Proverbs 27:10) ״רֵעֲךָ וְרֵעֶה אָבִיךָ״ etc., and the soul is to be compared to the garment by way of what they said in tractate Shabbat (152b): a parable to a king who distributed garments of royalty, etc. And we have already explained therein that since the soul of man is from the light of the Blessed One, as it is said of Him (Psalms 104:2) ״עוֹטֶה אוֹר כַּשַּׂלְמָה״, HaShem commanded that if it is held in pledge through debt — which is to say, its sins — there is time to restore it until the sun comes, by way of the verse (Psalms 90:3) ״תָּשֵׁב אֱנוֹשׁ עַד דַּכָּא״, and they said of blessed memory (Ecclesiastes Rabbah ch. 2): until the crushing of death, for there is time for repentance until the arrival of his sun." "And the reason for the doubling of <b>חָבֹל תַּחְבֹּל</b>: know that every person of Israel has three levels — nefesh, ru'aḥ, neshamah — and here Scripture alluded to all three of them. Corresponding to the neshamah He said <b>אִם חָבֹל</b>; corresponding to the ru'aḥ He said <b>תַּחְבֹּל</b>; and corresponding to the nefesh He said <b>שַׂלְמַת רֵעֶךָ</b>. And corresponding to them He said three divisions: first, <b>כִּי הִיא כְסוּתֹה לְבַדָּהּ</b> — that is the neshamah; second, <b>הִיא שִׂמְלָתוֹ לְעוֹרוֹ</b> — that is the ru'aḥ; third, <b>בַּמֶּה יִשְׁכָּב</b> — that is the nefesh that is with him in the grave, as it says (Job 14:22) ״וְנַפְשׁוֹ עָלָיו תֶּאֱבָל״." "And His saying <b>וְהָיָה כִּי יִצְעַק</b> — meaning, it returns to the first matter: ״תְּשִׁיבֶנּוּ לוֹ״, which is the restoration, for he will not need to exert himself to restore it; rather, ״כִּי יִצְעַק״ — HaShem will hear etc., and his sins will pass away."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:32:38.037396433Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}